  "narrative": "At synthesis, independent validation resolves four deadlines. H39 is accepted: MSI-high cells in adherent culture show much stronger WRN dependency; signed discovery +0.816 and validation +0.754 have lower bounds above +0.694, far above clinically meaningful magnitude. H31 is rejected: the apparent amplification of the MSI-high WRN effect in adherent versus nonadherent cells was not replicated; validation signed +0.024 [-0.087, +0.134]. H55 is rejected: MYC amplification is not meaningfully associated with stronger KIF18A dependency; signed estimates +0.009 and +0.013 are clinically trivial and intervals include zero. H75 is rejected: the original claim of weaker MDM2 dependency in CDKN2A-loss cells is opposite to both discovery and validation. The reversed claim H120 is accepted: CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency; signed estimates +0.119 and +0.153, validation interval +0.097 to +0.209, are directionally replicated and large relative to the MDM2 score distribution. The validation lower bound is marginally near the 0.1 absolute benchmark, but the combined evidence is clearly meaningful and independent, so I accept this as a dataset-specific association rather than a causal or generalizable finding. The evidence-supported core contexts are: MSI-high implies stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss implies stronger SMARCA2 dependency; TP53 loss implies weaker USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss implies weaker NFE2L2 dependency; and CDKN2A loss implies stronger MDM2 dependency. Negative and failed-replication evidence supports specificity by rejecting receptor/kinase pathway contrasts, MYC effects, BRCA2 effects, MTAP main effects, STK11/RB1 effects, and many constructed-marker interactions. Remaining uncertainty is context and confounding for CDKN2A/MDM2, especially TP53 status and MTAP co-deletion. The most informative next analysis is to stratify and test interactions of the CDKN2A-MDM2 association by TP53 and MTAP status; if robust, use remaining validation budget for the strongest context-specific form, otherwise close it as narrow.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 synthesis: accepted H39 and H120; rejected H31, H55, and H75. Core validated dataset-specific associations are MSI-high stronger WRN dependency, SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency, TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency, KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency, and CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2 dependency. H31 adherence interaction and H55 MYC-KIF18A association failed replication/clinical magnitude and are closed. Reserve remaining validation requests for context-specific MDM2/CDKN2A checks after TP53 and MTAP stratification. Do not prioritize receptor/PI3K/TMED10 unless a new strong signal appears. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied data, not causal or generalizable claims."
