  "narrative": "The new results substantially clarify the CDKN2A loss / MDM2 dependency association and disfavor a simple MTAP-loss-specific explanation. H141 is precise: the signed estimate is +0.1117 [0.0702, 0.1532] in low-9p21 cells with MTAP retained. Because H141 was direction -1, this corresponds to more negative MDM2 dependency scores in CDKN2A-loss cells, i.e. stronger dependency. The effect is large relative to the MDM2 score distribution and excludes the null, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association. H142 is larger, +0.1743 [0.0862, 0.2624] in low-9p21 MTAP-loss cells. Its lower confidence bound is slightly below my informal 0.1-unit practical benchmark and the exposed cell is smaller, but the point estimate is large and the interval excludes zero; I accept it with caution as another dataset-specific subgroup association. Together, H141 and H142 indicate that the CDKN2A-MDM2 effect is present whether MTAP is retained or lost, so it is not clearly MTAP-specific. H143 directly tests that interaction and is not supported: +0.0626 [-0.0345, 0.1597] crosses zero and the point estimate is modest. I reject it and close it. H144 tests MTAP loss among CDKN2A-loss low-9p21 cells and is also unsupported: +0.0676 [-0.0237, 0.1588] crosses zero and is below the magnitude I would regard as clinically meaningful on this scale. H145, MTAP loss among all CDKN2A-WT cells, is essentially null: +0.0053 [-0.0181, 0.0286]. This is important for specificity: MTAP loss alone does not explain MDM2 dependency in this dataset. H146 confirms that the low-9p21 CDKN2A-MDM2 effect persists under high Cas9 activity: +0.1380 [0.0845, 0.1916], which I accept as technical robustness, not generalizability. The receptor and pathway exploration is otherwise uninformative. H24, KRAS mutation and dependency_KRAS within adenocarcinoma, is near null and opposite to a strong dependency interpretation given the signed interval; reject. H60, H61, H63, H64, and H147 are near-null or in non-supported directions for KRAS/BRAF bypass, ERBB2, STAT3, or PIK3CA relationships; reject and close. I also reassessed H128, H137, and H125 as closed rejects because the direct MTAP-specific amplification claims remain unsupported: H128 failed independent validation, and the new MTAP-stratified analyses plus the null H143 interaction do not support an MTAP-loss-specific CDKN2A-MDM2 effect. Residual uncertainty remains mainly from collinearity: CDKN2A loss is nearly equivalent to low 9p21 copy number in this dataset, and the complementary high-9p21 stratum is untestable because CDKN2A-loss exposure there is too rare. Also, the MTAP-loss subgroup is smaller and H142 is precise but has a lower bound near the practical threshold. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations among measured variables, not causal claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 appraise notes. CDKN2A-MDM2 specificity is now better resolved. Accepted: CDKN2A loss associated with stronger MDM2 dependency in low-9p21 MTAP-WT cells (H141), in low-9p21 MTAP-loss cells with caution (H142), and in low-9p21 high-Cas9 cells (H146). Rejected: MTAP interaction (H143, H137, H125), MTAP-only effect among CDKN2A-loss low-9p21 cells (H144), MTAP-only effect among CDKN2A-WT cells (H145), and H128 MTAP-specific CDKN2A claim after failed validation. Interpretation: the accepted CDKN2A-MDM2 association appears to be a broad CDKN2A/9p21-locus or copy-number-context association in this dataset, not a MTAP-loss-specific effect. Remaining main uncertainty is collinearity of CDKN2A loss with low 9p21 copy number and inability to test high-9p21 CDKN2A-loss cells. Receptor/pathway claims H24, H60, H61, H63, H64, H147 are closed as unsupported. No validation requests remain. Future work, if any, is lower priority: possible joint CDKN2A x TP53/co-deletion context checks, but current evidence is sufficient for a broad low-9p21/CDKN2A-MDM2 dataset-specific claim and against an MTAP-specific claim."
}

