  "narrative": "No assessments are due. Validation requests are exhausted, so this stage registers 12 new dataset-specific discovery comparisons without parent links. The first six proposals test whether the strongest accepted associations remain detectable in two important internal contexts: high-serum culture conditions and the dominant Avana CRISPR library. These are not reassessments of the parent claims; they are new context-specific claims that can either improve confidence that the association is broadly present across screen culture/technical settings or reveal that the parent association was context-dependent. Direction conventions are preserved from the accepted claims: for KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss, direction +1 means the exposed cells are expected to have less negative dependency scores, i.e. weaker dependency; for CDKN2A loss, SMARCA4 loss, and MSI-high status, direction -1 means exposed cells are expected to have more negative dependency scores, i.e. stronger dependency. If a high-serum or Avana context shows a large shift with an interval excluding the null, I would regard it as supportive context robustness in this dataset, but not as evidence of causality or generalizability beyond the supplied data. If the effect attenuates below the practical benchmark or crosses the null, the alternative interpretation is that the parent association may be partly driven by non-high-serum or non-Avana screens, by correlated genomic features, or by context-specific culture stress. The next six proposals target unresolved receptor, secretory-trafficking, bypass, and downstream-pathway hypotheses in focused populations. EGFR amplification is hypothesized to increase RIT1 dependency or TMED10 dependency in adenocarcinoma cells, reflected by more negative dependency scores, because amplified receptor signaling could increase reliance on RAS-like signaling or receptor-secretory trafficking; alternatives include no association or reduced dependency if amplification bypasses these nodes. ERBB2 amplification is hypothesized to weaken EGFR dependency in adenocarcinoma cells, reflected by less negative EGFR scores, because ERBB2 can supply receptor-signaling capacity; the alternatives are no bypass effect or co-dependency. ERBB2 amplification is also tested against TMED10 for the same secretory-load logic. BRAF V600E is hypothesized to weaken KRAS dependency in adenocarcinoma cells through downstream MAPK bypass, reflected by a less negative KRAS score; the alternative is no effect or increased pathway dependency. Finally, PIK3CA mutation in KRAS-mutant cells is hypothesized to weaken STAT3 dependency through downstream survival signaling, reflected by a less negative STAT3 score; alternatives include null or additive pathway activation. For these dependency outcomes, I treat roughly 0.025 absolute shift as a practical relevance benchmark given typical dependency-score scales, while the accepted strong associations are much larger. All proposed conclusions will be interpreted only as associations among measured variables in this supplied dataset, not causal dependencies or externally generalizable clinical predictions."
