  "narrative": "No response-deadline assessments were due, and no new independent validation response was listed. The validation request budget is exhausted, so no further voluntary validation can be requested. I therefore synthesize the full set of discovery and previously delivered validation evidence already recorded in the ledger. All statements below are associations among measured variables in this supplied lung cell-line CRISPR dataset. They are not causal claims and they do not establish external generalizability.\n\nSIGN CONVENTIONS AND PRACTICAL SCALE. Returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction; a positive signed estimate supports the registered claim. For MSI-high/WRN, SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, and CDKN2A-loss/MDM2, direction is -1, so a positive signed estimate means exposed cells have more negative dependency scores, i.e. stronger dependency. For KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 and TP53-loss/USP7, direction is +1, so a positive signed estimate means exposed cells have less negative scores, i.e. weaker dependency. The stated practical threshold is a relative difference of at least 10%. The core supported effects are very large relative to the observed outcome scales, especially the approximately 0.75 to 0.81 unit differences on outcomes with means near zero and SDs roughly 0.25 to 0.37. The CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 effect is smaller in absolute units but still meaningful: about 0.12 to 0.15 units, roughly 45% to 60% of the mean absolute MDM2 dependency score.\n\nSUPPORTED DATASET-SPECIFIC FINDINGS.\n1. MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency. The overall supported estimate is +0.790, interval +0.760 to +0.820, with independent validation +0.797, +0.744 to +0.850. Context checks are consistently large and positive: adenocarcinoma +0.784, library_ky +0.751, adherent culture +0.816 with validation +0.754, high Cas9 activity +0.789, higher mutation burden +0.785, batch_a +0.815, serum >=10% +0.787, and low serum <=5% +0.794. Interaction tests against lineage subtype, research marker E, library_ky, culture, and Cas9 activity were null or imprecise. CDKN2A loss and SMARCA4 loss did not support WRN dependency, supporting outcome specificity.\n\n2. SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency. The overall supported estimate is +0.782, interval +0.761 to +0.802, with validation +0.805, +0.775 to +0.836. Context checks remain large: adenocarcinoma +0.775, library_ky +0.814, adherent culture +0.786, high Cas9 +0.785, ARID1A-loss stratum +0.805, EMT-high +0.767, batch_a +0.749, serum >=10% +0.796, low serum +0.760, and ARID1A-wildtype cells +0.776, interval +0.754 to +0.798. Interaction tests were null. ARID1A loss alone showed no robust SMARCA2 effect, CDKN2A loss showed no meaningful SMARCA2 effect, and BRCA2-loss tests were inconsistent with validation reversal. This supports SMARCA4 as the specific genomic predictor, not adjacent chromatin or DNA-repair markers.\n\n3. KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency. The overall supported estimate is +0.797, interval +0.776 to +0.819, with validation +0.804, +0.773 to +0.835. Direction and magnitude are stable in TP53-wildtype cells +0.789, adenocarcinoma +0.795, library_ky +0.787, adherent culture +0.795, batch_a +0.815, high Cas9 +0.795, serum >=10% +0.817, and low serum +0.771. Interactions with lineage subtype, research marker D, library_ky, culture, STK11 loss, MYC amplification, TP53 loss, and Cas9 activity were null. Cross-marker tests show that KEAP1 loss does not robustly affect WRN, SMARCA2, or MDM2, and TP53 loss does not robustly affect NFE2L2.\n\n4. TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency. The overall supported estimate is +0.804, interval +0.783 to +0.825, with validation +0.800, +0.768 to +0.831. Contexts include adenocarcinoma +0.803, library_ky +0.769, adherent culture +0.803, MTAP-loss +0.758, MTAP-wildtype +0.815, CDKN2A-wildtype +0.802, high Cas9 +0.807, batch_a +0.796, serum >=10% +0.804, and low serum +0.803. Interactions with CDKN2A loss, SMARCA4 loss, and Cas9 activity were null. TP53 loss was not robustly associated with NFE2L2, WRN, SMARCA2, MDM2, POLR2A, or RPL11 at meaningful scale, so USP7 is the specific TP53-associated outcome among tested dependency scores.\n\n5. CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency. The best-supported overall claim is +0.119, interval +0.083 to +0.155, with validation +0.153, +0.097 to +0.209. The effect is broad but smaller than the core synthetic-lethal-scale associations. It is also validated in TP53-wildtype cells: +0.119, interval +0.061 to +0.177. Additional contexts support the association: TP53-loss cells +0.121, MTAP-wildtype +0.106, TP53-wildtype MTAP-wildtype +0.104, low 9p21 copy number +0.125, low-9p21 MTAP-wildtype +0.112, low-9p21 MTAP-loss +0.174, Avana library +0.118, batch_a +0.119, high aneuploidy +0.134, high Cas9 +0.135, serum >=10% +0.124, and low serum +0.112. Interaction tests with TP53 loss, MTAP loss, and low-9p21 context were null, indicating no strong subgroup modification within the tested contexts. CDKN2A loss did not affect WRN or SMARCA2, supporting MDM2 specificity.\n\nVALIDATION STATUS. No new validation was due in this synthesis. Available validation supports the accepted core findings and supports null or negative interpretation for several earlier candidate associations. In particular, validation supports WRN-MSI-high, SMARCA2-SMARCA4 loss, NFE2L2-KEAP1 loss, USP7-TP53 loss, and the broad CDKN2A-MDM2 association including the TP53-wildtype stratum. Validation was null or inconsistent for EGFR amplification/EGFR dependency, the WRN MSI culture-type interaction, KIF18A MYC amplification, and BRCA2-loss/SMARCA2. The narrow TP53-wildtype MTAP-loss CDKN2A subgroup remains unresolved because discovery was imprecise and validation crossed zero. Because validation budget is exhausted, further acceptance depends on the strength, consistency, uncertainty, and practical magnitude of already delivered evidence.\n\nNEGATIVE OR UNSUPPORTED FINDINGS. Direct oncogene dependency hypotheses were not robustly supported. KRAS mutation was not associated with stronger KRAS dependency, including in a clean context excluding co-occurring BRAF, EGFR, and ERBB2 alterations; the clean-context estimate was +0.009, interval -0.011 to +0.030. BRAF V600E was not associated with stronger BRAF dependency in the clean context, estimate -0.030, interval -0.064 to +0.004. EGFR amplification was inconsistent, and the clean-context EGFR test was imprecise and below reliable practical significance: +0.022, interval -0.013 to +0.056. ERBB2 amplification was negligible in the clean context: -0.007, interval -0.045 to +0.032. Cross-receptor specificity checks were also null. Downstream STAT3 tests with KRAS mutation, EGFR amplification, and ERBB2 amplification did not support stronger STAT3 dependency. The only nominally significant interval in that block was the EGFR amplification/STAT3 test, but it was opposite the registered claim, barely excluded zero, not validated, and multiplicity-prone across many EGFR-pathway tests; it is treated as unsupported rather than as a supported reversal. RIT1 dependency showed no robust association with KRAS mutation, BRAF V600E, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, or clean KRAS mutation contexts. TMED10 showed no robust association with EGFR or ERBB2 amplification in adenocarcinoma. NF1 loss in driver-free cells did not support KRAS dependency.\n\nMany additional non-core genomic and constructed predictors were negative or negligible. MYC amplification did not robustly affect DHX9, KIF18A, POLR2A, or USP7. BRCA2 loss did not robustly affect DHX9, POLR2A, KIF18A, WRN, or SMARCA2, and SMARCA2 validation reversed. RB1 loss did not support KIF18A dependency. STK11 loss did not support WRN, SMARCA2, or NFE2L2 associations or interactions. PTEN loss did not support USP7. MTAP loss alone did not robustly affect MDM2 or USP7, and MTAP interaction tests were null. MSI-high did not support MDM2 dependency. KEAP1 loss did not support MDM2 dependency. TP53 loss did not support NFE2L2, WRN, SMARCA2, MDM2, POLR2A, RPL11, DHX9, or KIF18A at accepted practical scale. Research markers D, E, and F showed no meaningful main effects or interactions for the accepted core outcomes. Several small nominal findings were not accepted because their intervals were near zero, effects were around or below the practical threshold, they were unvalidated, or they were inconsistent with related tests.\n\nUNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY. The principal unresolved biological boundary is CDKN2A versus the 9p21 copy-number context. CDKN2A loss is tightly linked to low 9p21 copy number, and the complementary high-9p21 CDKN2A-loss stratum is essentially untestable because exposed cells are too rare. The evidence supports a broad CDKN2A/9p21 locus association with MDM2 dependency, but cannot cleanly separate CDKN2A gene loss from broader 9p21 copy-number effects. The TP53-wildtype MTAP-loss CDKN2A-loss subgroup also remains inconclusive. More broadly, accepted associations could reflect synthetic-lethal biology, copy-number effects, locus effects, assay library or culture context, correlated genomic features, or other measured or unmeasured confounding. Internal validation reduces random-error uncertainty but does not establish external replication or causality.\n\nCLOSED LOW-PRIORITY BRANCHES. I record investigation-only closures for the remaining untested deferred branches H50, H77, H78, H79, H80, H93, and H94. Their scientific status remains unresolved because no direct evidence was produced. The closure is administrative: the validation budget is exhausted, related pathway and downstream tests have been overwhelmingly null or imprecise, and these branches are now lower priority than the supported core findings.\n\nMOST INFORMATIVE NEXT ANALYSIS. The within-dataset subgroup splitting for the accepted core pairs has strong diminishing returns. The highest-value next work would use external replication and mechanistic perturbation: rescue or restore CDKN2A in CDKN2A-loss or 9p21-low lines to test MDM2 dependency specificity; test whether low 9p21 copy number remains associated with MDM2 after CDKN2A status is fixed; perform perturbation or rescue for KEAP1, TP53, SMARCA4, MSI context, WRN, and their associated dependency scores to establish causal direction; and populate rare strata such as high-9p21 CDKN2A-loss cells and TP53-wildtype MTAP-loss CDKN2A-loss cells. If limited to this dataset only, a pre-specified multivariable adjustment for 9p21 copy number, mutation burden, ploidy, Cas9 activity, media serum, CRISPR library, and batch would be more useful than further post-hoc splits. I therefore register no new dataset-specific comparisons and leave the accepted core findings unchanged.",
  "research_notes": "FINAL NOTEBOOK. No validation budget remains; no due response deadlines. Core accepted dataset-specific associations: MSI-high associated with stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4-loss associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1-loss associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; TP53-loss associated with weaker USP7 dependency; CDKN2A-loss associated with stronger MDM2 dependency. These associations are large, internally replicated across contexts, and in several cases independently validated within the supplied evidence framework. Direct oncogene, receptor, downstream pathway, many genomic, research-marker, and interaction hypotheses remain rejected, null, imprecise, or unresolved without meaningful support. Closed remaining deferred untested branches H50, H77-H80, H93-H94 as low priority without changing their unresolved scientific status. If resources become available, the highest-value next analyses are external replication and mechanistic perturbation/rescue of each accepted pair, plus population of rare CDKN2A high-9p21 and TP53-wildtype MTAP-loss strata. If limited to this dataset, stop random subgroup splits; use pre-specified multivariable adjustment or rare-stratum population. No new comparisons are registered because the most informative dataset-only branches are exhausted."
}

