  "assessments": [],
  "narrative": "No assessments are due, so no claim status is changed. Independent validation budget is exhausted, so the remaining value is targeted within-dataset association refinement rather than new causal inference or generalizability claims. The accepted core dataset associations are large and clinically relevant relative to the observed outcome scales: MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency, SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, and CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency. The weakest and most uncertain core association is CDKN2A loss with MDM2 dependency, which is also confounded by 9p21 copy-number status. I therefore register one interaction test for CDKN2A/MDM2 comparing the severe low-9p21 region with the rest of the eligible population, plus a low-screen-quality direct test for CDKN2A/MDM2. These are intended to ask whether the CDKN2A/MDM2 effect is stable when screen quality is poor and whether it is markedly stronger where 9p21 copy number is deeply low. For the interaction claim, the anticipated direction is uncertain: a near-null interaction would support effect stability across copy-number context, whereas a large signed interaction would suggest locus-level confounding. For all mean-difference refinements, the direction is the accepted hypothesis sign. The expected raw contrast follows the accepted main effect: positive raw exposed-minus-comparator contrasts for TP53 loss with USP7 and KEAP1 loss with NFE2L2 because those accepted effects represent weaker dependency, and negative raw contrasts for SMARCA4 loss with SMARCA2, MSI-high with WRN, and CDKN2A loss with MDM2 because those accepted effects represent stronger dependency. Low Cas9 activity and Avana-library strata are not new random subgroup exploration; they are pre-specified robustness checks against editing-quality and library-assay artifacts. Low Cas9 direct tests quantify effect size when Cas9 activity is below the midpoint rather than only in high-activity cells. Avana direct tests confirm that the core associations are not confined to the minority Ky library and are not artifacts of overall pooling across libraries. Low-screen-quality testing for CDKN2A/MDM2 checks whether the weaker but practically meaningful MDM2 association survives in poorer CRISPR screen-quality quartiles. All returned estimates will already be signed to the stated direction and must be interpreted as observed associations within this supplied lung cancer cell-line dataset, not as proof of causality, synthetic lethality, rescue, or external clinical generalizability. Rare strata may remain underpowered or fail the minimum-cell diagnostic; those should be closed or left unresolved rather than overinterpreted.",
  "research_notes": "ITERATION 16 EXPLORATION NOTE: Validation budget is exhausted, so future work is dataset-specific robustness and locus-confounding analysis. Accepted core associations: MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency; CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency, but with unresolved CDKN2A versus 9p21 copy-number context. Direct oncogene-dependency hypotheses and most noncore markers were negative or negligible. Registered 11 targeted new claims: CDKN2A/MDM2 interaction by severe low 9p21 copy number; CDKN2A/MDM2 low-screen-quality direct effect; low Cas9 activity direct effects for TP53/USP7, KEAP1/NFE2L2, SMARCA4/SMARCA2, MSI/WRN, and CDKN2A/MDM2; Avana-library direct effects for TP53/USP7, KEAP1/NFE2L2, SMARCA4/SMARCA2, and MSI/WRN. Priority for analyze and appraise: CDKN2A/MDM2 severe-9p21 interaction, CDKN2A low Cas9, and CDKN2A low screen quality first because they address the weakest and most confounded accepted association. Core library and low-Cas9 tests are secondary robustness checks. If CDKN2A/MDM2 remains directionally consistent with clinically meaningful relative effect in low-screen and low-Cas9 contexts, the association is less likely to be an assay artifact. If the severe-9p21 interaction is near null, CDKN2A gene loss may be operating beyond local 9p21 copy number; if the interaction is large, 9p21 copy-number confounding remains likely. If low-Cas9 or Avana contexts are null or underpowered, interpret cautiously and close unresolved rare strata. These analyses remain observational and dataset-specific."
}

