  "narrative": "The new batch is dominated by strong robustness evidence for the four large core associations. In low-Cas9 cells, TP53 loss remained associated with much weaker USP7 dependency (R194, signed +0.810, 95% CI +0.773 to +0.846), KEAP1 loss with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency (R195, +0.802, +0.761 to +0.842), SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (R196, signed +0.767, +0.731 to +0.804), and MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency (R197, +0.815, +0.767 to +0.864). In the dominant Avana library, all four effects were similarly large and tight (R199-R202). These are not causal tests, but they strongly reduce the concern that the core associations are artifacts of high editing activity, minority library pooling, or random subgroup selection. H196, the severe low-9p21 interaction test for CDKN2A/MDM2, is near zero but very wide (R193, +0.005, -0.171 to +0.162) with only 25 exposed cells in the deep-copy-number subgroup; it is inconclusive for locus-context modification and remains unresolved/closed. For CDKN2A/MDM2, H201 shows the association remains in low-Cas9 cells with a signed effect +0.089 (95% CI +0.030 to +0.147), whose lower bound is around the practical scale used for MDM2 (~10% of the mean absolute MDM2 score), so I accept it with an attenuation caveat. H206 is more equivocal: in lower screen-quality cells, the point estimate is +0.076 and the interval excludes zero, but the lower bound is only +0.007, below a clinically meaningful scale; this is insufficient precision to accept a scientifically meaningful retained effect, so it remains unresolved/closed. Multiplicity is moderate but the large effects are pre-specified robustness checks, and no validation budget remains for additional independent confirmation.",
  "research_notes": "ITERATION 16 APPRAISE: Low-Cas9 and Avana-library tests strongly support the four large core associations: TP53-loss/USP7 weaker dependency, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 weaker dependency, SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 stronger dependency, and MSI-high/WRN stronger dependency. These are dataset associations, not causality or external generalizability. CDKN2A/MDM2 remains the most fragile accepted association: it survives in low Cas9 (R198) but is only directionally suggestive in low screen quality (R203, CI lower bound near zero), and the severe low-9p21 interaction is inconclusive (R193, wide, 25 exposed cells). Therefore CDKN2A vs 9p21/locus confounding remains unresolved. No new validation requests are possible. No further random subgroup exploration is planned. Final emphasis: four large robust associations are well supported in this dataset; CDKN2A/MDM2 is supported but smaller and locus-confounded; oncogene direct-dependency hypotheses remain unsupported."
}

