  "narrative": "Final synthesis. No response-deadline assessments were due, no newly released validation evidence changed the controller-maintained accepted set, and the independent-validation budget is exhausted; therefore I do not change any claim status or propose further dataset comparisons. Practical scale: dependency scores are more negative for stronger dependency. Returned signed estimates are interpreted in the claim direction. A practical difference was judged relative to the observed outcome scale, approximately 10 percent of mean absolute magnitude; the four core effects are far above that threshold, and the CDKN2A-loss MDM2 effect is also above the approximate threshold though smaller. Supported dataset-specific associations. First, MSI-high cells show stronger WRN dependency; discovery and independent validation produce large stable signed effects near 0.79 to 0.80, and context tests across lineage, culture, library, Cas9 activity, media serum, mutation burden, batch, and specificity checks are consistent. Second, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, with discovery near 0.78 and validation near 0.81, stable across many measured contexts and with null modification tests. Third, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, signed effect near 0.80, meaning less negative NFE2L2 scores, robust across contexts. Fourth, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency, near 0.80, robust across contexts. Fifth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, near 0.12 in discovery and 0.15 in validation, supported in TP53 wild type and loss, MTAP wild type, low 9p21 copy-number contexts, multiple libraries, media serum, Cas9-activity strata, and mutation-burden contexts. It is accepted as clinically or practically meaningful on the MDM2 scale, but it is the smallest and most locus-confounded accepted effect. Negative findings. Direct oncogene dependence was not supported: KRAS mutation was not associated with stronger KRAS dependency, BRAF V600E was not associated with stronger BRAF dependency in driver-clean context, EGFR amplification was inconsistent and not accepted for EGFR dependency, ERBB2 amplification was negligible for ERBB2 dependency, and RIT1 dependency did not track measured drivers. Cross-receptor checks, STAT3 downstream probes, TMED10 probes, MYC amplification, BRCA2 loss, RB1 loss, STK11 loss, PTEN loss, MTAP loss as a main effect, and constructed research markers D, E, and F were generally null or not supported. Some independent validation actively argued against candidate claims: EGFR-amplification EGFR dependency, BRCA2-loss SMARCA2 dependency, and culture interaction for WRN MSI-high were not accepted, and the TP53-wildtype MTAP-loss CDKN2A MDM2 subgroup remained unresolved after validation. Unresolved uncertainty. The CDKN2A-MDM2 finding cannot be cleanly separated from broader 9p21 copy-number loss, MTAP effects, aneuploidy, or correlated genomic features. Rare or low-quality strata, especially Humagne-CD library, low Cas9-activity screens, severe 9p21 interactions, and small low-mutation-burden MSI-high cells remain imprecise. Interaction tests mostly establish no strong detected modification but cannot exclude moderate context effects. More broadly, all accepted results are associations within the supplied lung cell-line dataset, not causal synthetic-lethality claims or external generalizability. Most informative next analysis. The highest-value follow-up is external and mechanistic: replicate the four large associations in independent CRISPR screens; rescue or restore CDKN2A or test 9p21 copy number with CDKN2A status fixed to determine whether MDM2 dependency is gene-specific; perturb or rescue KEAP1, TP53, SMARCA4, and MSI context; populate rare library and high-9p21 CDKN2A-loss contexts; and use pre-specified adjusted models with 9p21 copy number, mutation burden, ploidy, Cas9 activity, screen quality, media serum, library, and batch. Further post-hoc subgroup splitting in this dataset would add little, especially with no validation budget remaining.",
