sh the registered directional interactions, so I reject them. H233, H235, and H236 do not support PTEN loss predicting stronger MDM2 dependency. H233 is signed opposite the hypothesis and small (-0.021, 95% CI [-0.050, +0.009]); H235 is also signed opposite in TP53-intact cells (-0.026, 95% CI [-0.059, +0.007]); H236 is imprecise and small in the TP53-mutant interaction (+0.025, 95% CI [-0.050, +0.100]). H234 gives only a negligible positive effect for PIK3CA mutation with MDM2 dependency (+0.008, 95% CI [-0.020, +0.037]). Thus the PI3K/PTEN/PIK3CA-MDM2 probes are closed as unsupported directional associations. The remaining STAT3 probes and MYC-RPL11 probe are null or negligible: H241 is small and opposite-signed (-0.009, 95% CI [-0.037, +0.019]); H242 and H243 are small with intervals spanning null; H244 is negligible and opposite-signed. I reject all of these. No new validation can be requested. I do not register further arbitrary subgroup analyses, because doing so would increase multiplicity without adding decisive evidence; the most scientifically informative next step would be independent replication of PTEN loss-STAT3 with adjustment for correlated genomic lesions, followed by mechanistic perturbation or rescue studies.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 21 appraise complete. Validation request budget is exhausted, so no independent validation can be requested. Final panel conclusions: PTEN loss-STAT3 remains accepted only as a large, precise within-dataset discovery association; H237 PIK3CA-intact stratum and H240 adenocarcinoma stratum provide robustness support and are accepted/closed. PTEN loss does not support stronger MDM2 dependency overall, in TP53-intact cells, or as a TP53-mutant interaction; PIK3CA mutation-MDM2 is negligible. PTEN loss-STAT3 interaction by media serum or mutation burden is not supported, although these tests do not prove homogeneity. STAT3 associations with ARID1A loss, SMAD4 loss, MSI-high, and MYC amplification effect on RPL11 are null or too small and are rejected/closed. Accepted within-dataset associations remain MSI-high-WRN, SMARCA4 loss-SMARCA2, KEAP1 loss-NFE2L2, TP53 loss-USP7, CDKN2A loss-MDM2, and PTEN loss-STAT3. The latter is the newest and is discovery-only. Avoid further post-hoc subgroup mining; future work should focus on external validation and mechanistic testing, especially for PTEN loss-STAT3 and for separating CDKN2A/MTAP/9p21 confounding."
