  "narrative": "No assessments are due and validation requests are exhausted, so this stage registers a focused discovery-only panel that refines accepted conclusions without changing them. The panel has two parts. First, it tests specificity and pleiotropy: whether canonical accepted markers SMARCA4 loss, KEAP1 loss, TP53 loss, and CDKN2A loss show large effects on STAT3 dependency, and whether PTEN loss shows large effects on noncanonical outcomes WRN, SMARCA2, and NFE2L2. If these are near null or small, the accepted associations are more outcome-specific; if they approach the magnitudes of the accepted core effects, that would argue for broader genomic or screen-level confounding rather than targeted dependency biology. Direction choices for specificity tests reflect the accepted direction for the marker on its own canonical outcome: SMARCA4 and CDKN2A accepted directions are stronger dependency, while KEAP1 and TP53 accepted directions are weaker dependency; for PTEN pleiotropy, the direction is stronger dependency because the accepted PTEN-STAT3 effect is stronger dependency. These are tests, not assumptions, so anticipated_direction is 0. Second, it tests growth-rate modification of the accepted core associations and PTEN-STAT3 using the median growth-rate split, growth_rate_doublings_per_day >= 0.462. Growth rate is a plausible source of dependency-score scale differences because proliferation can shape CRISPR screen dynamics. Near-null interactions would support stability across growth contexts; large interactions would indicate context dependence. The eligibility and subgroup variables are distinct, with only has_crispr_qc and has_dna_omics as eligibility and growth_rate_doublings_per_day only in the subgroup. All claims are within-dataset associations. For direction -1, a positive signed estimate indicates a more negative, i.e. stronger, dependency in the exposed group relative to the comparator; for direction 1, a positive signed estimate indicates a less negative, i.e. weaker, dependency. Interactions compare the exposed-minus-comparator contrast in the subgroup with that in the complement. I will promote only effects with precise intervals and magnitudes clearly beyond noise and plausibly clinically relevant on the dependency-score scale; small, imprecise, or context-only signals will not be promoted.",
  "research_notes": "Discovery-only refinement panel after validation budget exhausted. No due assessments. Registered 12 claims: 7 specificity/pleiotropy tests and 5 growth-rate interaction tests. Specificity/pleiotropy: canonical markers on STAT3 (SMARCA4, KEAP1, TP53, CDKN2A) and PTEN on WRN/SMARCA2/NFE2L2. Growth-rate interactions: median split growth_rate_doublings_per_day >= 0.462 for MSI-high-WRN, SMARCA4-SMARCA2, KEAP1-NFE2L2, TP53-USP7, PTEN-STAT3. Parent links: H11, H12, H13, H48, H230. Interpret signed estimates by registered direction; positive signed estimates support the registered direction. For direction -1, stronger dependency; for direction 1, weaker dependency. Promote only large/precise effects. These tests refine outcome specificity and robustness; they do not establish causality or external generalizability. If specificity tests are large, accepted associations may reflect broad genomic/screen confounding. If growth interactions are large, accepted associations are growth-context dependent; if null, stability is supported."
}

