  "narrative": "All 12 new refinement tests are within-dataset association tests using measured baseline predictors or screen-quality growth proxies; there is no apparent outcome leakage because exposure variables are not post-outcome transformations. I interpret returned estimates as already signed to the registered direction: for direction -1, positive signed estimates would support stronger exposed-group dependency, while for direction +1 positive signed estimates support weaker exposed-group dependency; interactions follow the same signed convention for the contrast difference. The evidence does not support any of the registered H245-H256 directional hypotheses. For the specificity/pleiotropy panel, SMARCA4 loss has a negligible opposite-signed STAT3 effect (-0.008, 95% CI -0.037 to +0.021), KEAP1 loss a small opposite-signed STAT3 effect (-0.020, 95% CI -0.050 to +0.010), TP53 loss a negligible same-signed STAT3 effect (+0.008, 95% CI -0.019 to +0.034), and CDKN2A loss a negligible opposite-signed STAT3 effect (-0.006, 95% CI -0.033 to +0.022). PTEN loss also does not show large effects on noncanonical outcomes: WRN +0.002 (95% CI -0.034 to +0.039), SMARCA2 +0.027 (95% CI -0.022 to +0.077), and NFE2L2 -0.038 (95% CI -0.088 to +0.013). These results favor outcome specificity rather than broad marker-level dependency effects, although they do not prove absence of pleiotropy because residual confounding by correlated genomic lesions remains. For growth-rate modification, all interactions are compatible with no modification or too imprecise/weak to promote: MSI-high WRN interaction -0.051 (95% CI -0.117 to +0.016), SMARCA4 SMARCA2 interaction -0.032 (95% CI -0.078 to +0.015), KEAP1 NFE2L2 interaction +0.032 (95% CI -0.014 to +0.079), TP53 USP7 interaction +0.000 (95% CI -0.045 to +0.046), and PTEN STAT3 interaction +0.013 (95% CI -0.107 to +0.133). None reaches a scientifically meaningful magnitude, and many intervals include zero and modest opposite-direction values. Given the multiplicity of subgroup/interaction testing, I reject all due claims and close these refinement investigations. Independent validation cannot be requested because the validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Appraised H245-H256 and closed all as rejected. Specificity/pleiotropy tests are null or negligible for canonical markers on STAT3 and for PTEN loss on WRN/SMARCA2/NFE2L2, supporting outcome specificity but not proving causality. Growth-rate interaction tests are broadly null, supporting stability of accepted core associations across proliferation-rate contexts, though intervals are not always tight. No new claims registered. Validation budget exhausted; further dataset subgrouping would increase multiplicity without likely decisive evidence. Future work should use external cohorts, multivariable adjustment for correlated lesions and screen parameters, and mechanistic rescue/inhibition studies.",
