  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation budget is exhausted, so this final explore stage registers discovery-only refinements and focused new associations. For direction -1, a positive signed mean_difference means the exposed group has a more negative, i.e., stronger, dependency score. For direction +1, a positive signed mean_difference means the exposed group has a less negative, i.e., weaker, dependency score. For interactions, a positive signed interaction means the registered exposed-minus-comparator contrast is stronger in the named subgroup than in the complement. The highest-priority remaining uncertainty is the PTEN-loss association with stronger STAT3 dependency, which is large and internally robust across several within-dataset strata but was not independently validated. I therefore test whether PTEN-STAT3 persists in PI3K-mutant and TP53-mutant genomic contexts, whether it is enhanced in inflammatory/high-IFN states, and whether it is modified by high aneuploidy. I also test accepted core associations in new biological contexts: KEAP1-loss cells for the TP53-USP7 effect, TP53-loss cells for KEAP1-NFE2L2, fast-growing cells for MSI-high-WRN, STK11-loss cells for CDKN2A-MDM2, and high-stemness cells for SMARCA4-SMARCA2. I add a paralog hypothesis: ARID1A loss may associate with stronger SMARCA2 dependency specifically when SMARCA4 is intact, because SWI/SNF paralog compensation is expected to be context-dependent. Finally, I add two pathway hypotheses for STAT3: MYC amplification and STK11/LKB1 loss may each be associated with stronger STAT3 dependency through transcriptional/inflammatory cooperation. All proposals use discovery Welch tests with 95% intervals and require at least 20 observations in every comparison cell. These are associations within this lung line data, not causal or external claims.",
